Z||000013||SCCA FIERO||08-25-2000||08:37 PM||||Monkey, click start, then RUN, then type "MSCONFIG" and then enter.<P>Then click "startup" and uncheck the stuff you don't want running. I think I leared that from a post that Ciff did, so I guess he deserves credit   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>OK, I just reread your post, Monkey. I guess what I posted won't help. Try this (also learned from Cliff):Type "SYSMON" in the RUN thingy (technical term) and it will tell you what system resources are being used.<P>I tried the thing you mentioned, Monkey, and it didn't work for me. <P>:::slamming fist against computer:::<P>I don't know why.<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 08-25-2000).]||||reg||1
